# Admin UI design contract

When building or restyling any admin page, follow `/admin/users` as the reference.

## Layout

- Page head: eyebrow + title + subtitle only (no floating action cluster in the hero).
- Primary actions (**Import / Export / Add**) live in the **table toolbar**, next to quick search.
- Filters sit **above the table**, horizontal grid; **Apply / Reset below** the filter fields.
- Prefer **center Dialog** for View / Create / Edit — not right Drawer for long forms.
- Surfaces: translucent panel + `body-bg.jpg`; IBM Plex; base ≥ 16.5px / weight ≥ 500.

## Filters & table

- Filters: only fields that matter for that domain; use **MultiSelect** (chips) when multi-value helps.
- Table: **STT**, quick search, **sortable** columns, colored status/role pills, View + Edit + Delete.
- Export must respect **active filters** (server-side CSV via `useApiDownload` / native `fetch`).

## Import UX

- Clear steps: (1) download template → (2) drag-drop / pick file → (3) auto-validate result.
- Show file name, size, upload progress %; auto-run preview after file select (no separate “check” click).
- Confirm import only when `import_token` exists.

## CRUD + API discipline

- While designing a screen: call real APIs, exercise happy path + empty/error states, **fix bugs immediately**.
- Add missing backend endpoints in the same change when UI needs them (export/import/bulk/sort/multi-filter).
- All user-facing strings go through i18n (`vi` + `en`).

## Do not

- Copy old `frontend_superbackup` layout 1:1.
- Put long filter rails on the left.
- Ship stubs that claim features without wired APIs.
